# width: 120
# Splitting a rendered markdown tab. A markdown file opens rendered
# (`ui.markdown_opens_rendered`), and its split's companion is the
# file's SOURCE editor beside the rendering. Before 2026-09-22 the
# companion came back as the rendered tab itself — `openPath` routes a
# markdown file to its rendered tab — so the split took the only tab
# out of its leaf and then had no leaf to split: the layout emptied and
# the file was gone from both halves. This is the user's "I split and
# end up with nothing loaded", as a glance and as a kept tab.
write README.md "# hi\nsecond line\n"
write notes.md "# notes\nthird line\n"
command tree.refresh

# Rows (case-folded order): the workspace header 1, notes.md 2,
# README.md 3. One click: a rendered glance — the heading loses its #.
click 14 3
expect pane "README.md"
expect screen contains "second line"
expect screen lacks "# hi"
expect status contains "\"panes\":[{\"title\":\"README.md\",\"dirty\":false,\"preview\":true}]"

# The strip's split-right button (column 112 at 120 wide): the
# rendering stays, the source editor shows the raw heading beside it,
# and both tabs are kept.
click 112 1
expect pane "README.md"
expect screen contains "second line"
expect screen contains "# hi"
expect status contains "\"panes\":[{\"title\":\"README.md\",\"dirty\":false,\"preview\":false},{\"title\":\"README.md\",\"dirty\":false,\"preview\":false}]"
command view.close_split
expect pane "README.md"
expect screen contains "second line"

# A kept open of a markdown file (the double-click) splits down the
# same way: rendering above, source below, nothing lost.
doubleclick 14 2
expect pane "notes.md"
expect screen contains "third line"
expect screen lacks "# notes"
click 115 1
expect pane "notes.md"
expect screen contains "third line"
expect screen contains "# notes"
expect status lacks "\"preview\":true"
